# weechat — real-world examples

Terminal IRC client. On Tumbleweed: `sudo zypper in weechat`. Runs nicely
inside a tmux session on homelab so you never miss scrollback.

## Getting connected

```text
/server add libera irc.libera.chat/6697 -ssl
/connect libera
/join #opensuse
/nick david_hl
/quit
```

## Buffer navigation

```text
Ctrl-s Ctrl-u       Set unread marker on all windows
Ctrl-p, Alt-left    Switch buffer left
Ctrl-n, Alt-right   Switch buffer right
Alt-a               Jump to next buffer with activity
Alt-0...9           Switch to buffer 0-9
/buffer close       Close current buffer
```

## Scrolling

```text
PgUp/PgDn           Scroll buffer text
F9/F10              Scroll buffer title
F11/F12             Scroll nick list
Alt-u               Scroll to first unread line
```

## Everyday commands

```text
/query nick         Open a private chat
/msg nick hello     One-off private message
/topic              Show channel topic
/away brb coffee    Set away status
/save               Write config to disk
/set irc.look.*     Browse settings (tab-completes)
```

## Run it persistently on the homelab

```sh
# Start weechat inside tmux over ssh; detach with Ctrl-b d
ssh david@homelab
tmux new -s irc weechat

# Reattach later from any machine
tmux attach -t irc
```
